      "message": "Optional / follow-up note on `gr-copy-clipboard`: setting `multiline` reflects `[multiline]` on the host, which triggers `:host([multiline]) gr-button { margin-top: 0; }` in `gr-copy-clipboard.ts` (added in Ie2c39e1b for top-aligning with a visible `\u003ctextarea\u003e`). Because `gr-button` normally has `margin: calc(0px - var(--spacing-s))` (`-4px`) on all sides to cancel out its padding, setting `margin-top: 0` while `hideInput` is true makes the button\u0027s vertical margins asymmetric (`0` top vs `-4px` bottom) and shifts the copy icon down by ~2px relative to the adjacent `md-icon-button`.\n\nIt might be worth scoping those rules in `gr-copy-clipboard.ts` to `:host([multiline]:not([hideinput]))` (or having `GrCopyClipboard.copyToClipboard()` copy `this.text` directly rather than reading back `queryAndAssert(this, \u0027#input\u0027).value` from the hidden readonly input).\n\n_(from potto)_",
